now-it-all (negative)\n- has a hot temper (negative)\n\nNow evaluate against criteria: reliability/responsibility, technical competence, calmness/pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership => good for decision-making, technical, situational awareness. Negatives: show-off, not open to new ideas => may affect teamwork, adaptability, professional development. No info on stress handling, calmness. So mixed.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills => good reliability, stress, technical. Weak memory for numbers (could affect navigation), nasty remarks => teamwork problem. Not open to new ideas? Not mentioned. So strong reliability but teamwork issue.\n\nCandidate C: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands tech => good decision, calmness, technical. Negatives: communication difficulty, egocentric, unwilling to further education => teamwork and professional development issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected, concentration, problem solving, responsibility => strong reliability, technical problem solving, responsibility. Negatives: know-it-all, hot temper => teamwork and stress handling maybe. No info on calmness under pressure, but problem solving suggests competence.\n\nWe need provisional preference. Which candidate balances strengths and weaknesses best? For long-distance flights, calmness, decision-making, technical competence, teamwork crucial. Candidate C has calmness and quick decisions, but communication issues and egocentric may be problematic. Candidate B handles stress well, conscientious, good weather assessment, but nasty remarks harmful to crew. Candidate D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but hot temper may affect crew under stress. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but not open to new ideas and show-off may affect crew.\n\nWhich seems best? Possibly Candidate D: strong responsibility, problem solving, concentration, adequate response to unexpected events. Negatives: hot temper and know-it-all could affect teamwork, but maybe manageable? Candidate B's nasty remarks are severe for crew cooperation. Candidate C's communication difficulty is also severe. Candidate A's not open to new ideas may hinder adaptation to new tech.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate D, but with uncertainty due to hot temper and know-it-all attitude.\n\nWe should note what would change: evidence of strong teamwork/communication, or evidence that hot temper leads to unsafe decisions, or positive evidence about other candidates' teamwork.\n\nNow produce output."}
